From e9a7de802a90150460c751840910b42922d59946 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SOTA-PNU <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 19:29:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fpga/vcu118: drop the ISP (EnableIsp=0), add int8/f32 matmul
 benchmark

coralnpu_soc gains EnableIsp (default 1, Nexus unchanged). The VCU118 has no
camera; removing the ISP frees area and routing for the matrix variant and
removes the only hold violations (ISP async-reset removal paths).
---
 fpga/BUILD                    |   6 +
 fpga/rtl/chip_vcu118.sv       |   1 +
 fpga/rtl/coralnpu_soc.sv      | 288 ++++++++++++++++++++--------------
 fpga/sw/vcu118/matmul_bench.c | 173 ++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 352 insertions(+), 116 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 fpga/sw/vcu118/matmul_bench.c

